<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-04T13:19:00+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Sun, 04 Oct 2026 13:19:00 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Historic Atlanta mansion cut in half and moved to save it]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134671395.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Historic Randolph-Lucas-Jones House was saved from demolition by new owners who relocated it in 2013. Built in 1924 for a descendant of Thomas Jefferson, the house required significant restoration after moving. The removal involved careful dismantling of the structure to reduce weight and manage logistics effectively. Restoration efforts were extensive, demanding creative financial planning to ensure the project continued. The house honors preservation advocate Christopher M.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-atlanta-mansion-built-in-1924-for-thomas-jeffersons-great-great-grandson-faced-demolition-in-2013-its-new-owners-cut-the-8000-sq-ft-home-in-two-and-moved-it-about-2-miles-to-save-it/articleshow/134671395.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-atlanta-mansion-built-in-1924-for-thomas-jeffersons-great-great-grandson-faced-demolition-in-2013-its-new-owners-cut-the-8000-sq-ft-home-in-two-and-moved-it-about-2-miles-to-save-it/articleshow/134671395.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T13:07:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134671438,imgsize-243438.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UK collector's £15 teapot sold for £575,000 after experts identified rare Bartlam piece]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134670524.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A broken teapot bought for £15 at a 2016 auction was identified as a rare piece made by John Bartlam in South Carolina in the 1760s. It later sold for £460,000 at auction, reaching £575,000 with the buyer’s premium, and was acquired by The Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-uk-collector-paid-15-for-a-broken-lidless-teapot-at-a-2016-auction-experts-identified-it-as-one-of-only-seven-known-john-bartlam-pieces-and-it-sold-for-575000-to-the-met-in-new-york/articleshow/134670524.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-uk-collector-paid-15-for-a-broken-lidless-teapot-at-a-2016-auction-experts-identified-it-as-one-of-only-seven-known-john-bartlam-pieces-and-it-sold-for-575000-to-the-met-in-new-york/articleshow/134670524.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T12:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134670704,imgsize-38120.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Shonda Rhimes sells restored Hancock Park mansion for record $21 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134669899.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2014-shonda-rhimes-bought-a-1923-hancock-park-mansion-for-8-8-million-after-restoring-and-expanding-it-she-sold-the-12000-sq-ft-estate-for-a-record-21-million-in-2022/articleshow/134669899.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2014-shonda-rhimes-bought-a-1923-hancock-park-mansion-for-8-8-million-after-restoring-and-expanding-it-she-sold-the-12000-sq-ft-estate-for-a-record-21-million-in-2022/articleshow/134669899.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T13:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134669972,imgsize-846592.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Russia cuts education and healthcare budget as war spending hits new high]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134670322.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Russia's financial burden is not limited to military spending. The government is also spending more on servicing its debt as high interest rates increase borrowing costs. Debt-servicing costs in 2027 are expected to be 21.6% higher than originally planned. They are projected to account for 9.4% of total government spending next year and could rise further to 10.6% by 2029.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/russia-cuts-welfare-education-and-healthcare-budget-as-war-spending-hits-new-high/articleshow/134670322.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/russia-cuts-welfare-education-and-healthcare-budget-as-war-spending-hits-new-high/articleshow/134670322.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T11:51:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134670677,imgsize-68336.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Not afraid of death': Co-pilot's chilling admission after trying to crash flydubai jet]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134670774.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/not-afraid-of-death-co-pilots-chilling-admission-after-trying-to-crash-flydubai-jet/articleshow/134670774.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/not-afraid-of-death-co-pilots-chilling-admission-after-trying-to-crash-flydubai-jet/articleshow/134670774.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T12:05:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134670839,imgsize-90708.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Puerto Rico seventh-grader turns plantain peels into mulch, cutting weeds by up to 53%]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134657056.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Wileidy Feliciano-Rivera, a seventh-grader from Puerto Rico, transformed discarded plantain peels into biodegradable mulch. This innovative project addressed plastic waste and showcased potential agricultural benefits. EcoMusa, the resultant mulch, effectively reduced weed growth during testing while retaining moisture and lowering soil temperatures. Wileidy's work has garnered recognition as a finalist in the 2026 Thermo Fisher Scientific Junior Innovators Challenge.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-wileidy-feliciano-rivera-the-puerto-rico-seventh-grader-who-turned-discarded-school-cafeteria-plantain-peels-into-biodegradable-farm-mulch-that-cut-weed-growth-by-up-to-53-in-tests/articleshow/134657056.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-wileidy-feliciano-rivera-the-puerto-rico-seventh-grader-who-turned-discarded-school-cafeteria-plantain-peels-into-biodegradable-farm-mulch-that-cut-weed-growth-by-up-to-53-in-tests/articleshow/134657056.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T11:56:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134657159,imgsize-647257.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Mojave Desert search finds 6 new bee population groups; why tiny poppy specialist escaped endangered listing]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134656554.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Recent surveys have revealed six new population groups of the Mojave poppy bee, surprising biologists with the species’ extended range and resilience. Despite this positive news, a population group in Utah was unfortunately noted as lost. Findings suggest that the Mojave poppy bee does not currently warrant protection under the Endangered Species Act, but conservation efforts will persist to enhance its habitat monitoring.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/us-biologists-searching-the-mojave-desert-found-six-previously-unknown-mojave-poppy-bee-population-groups-the-new-evidence-helped-determine-the-tiny-specialist-bee-does-not-need-endangered-species-listing/articleshow/134656554.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/us-biologists-searching-the-mojave-desert-found-six-previously-unknown-mojave-poppy-bee-population-groups-the-new-evidence-helped-determine-the-tiny-specialist-bee-does-not-need-endangered-species-listing/articleshow/134656554.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T11:56:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134656935,imgsize-602069.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[NSW planted bitou bush to stabilise dunes; it now threatens native ecosystems across 46% of coast]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134656149.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Bitou bush was intentionally planted along the New South Wales coast to stabilize sand dunes. This plant has since spread extensively, covering 46% of the coastline and threatening native vegetation. Infestations of bitou bush replace native plant species and alter animal habitats throughout the region. A Threat Abatement Plan has been established to manage and contain this invasive species effectively.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/from-1946-nsw-planted-south-african-bitou-bush-to-stabilise-coastal-sand-dunes-decades-later-it-had-spread-along-46-of-the-states-coastline-and-threatened-native-ecosystems/articleshow/134656149.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/from-1946-nsw-planted-south-african-bitou-bush-to-stabilise-coastal-sand-dunes-decades-later-it-had-spread-along-46-of-the-states-coastline-and-threatened-native-ecosystems/articleshow/134656149.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T10:55:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134656235,imgsize-2242157.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sydney shopper’s A$4 cup turns out to be worth A$75,640]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134656341.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A shopper discovered a unique Chinese libation cup at a thrift shop in Sydney, Australia. They bought the cup for A$4 despite its significant chip. After assessing the item, a Sotheby's specialist appraised it at A$20,000 to A$30,000. The item was later auctioned for A$75,640, significantly exceeding the original purchase price. This event highlights the potential hidden value in thrift store finds.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-sydney-shopper-bought-a-carved-cup-for-a4-at-a-thrift-shop-experts-identified-it-as-a-centuries-old-chinese-rhinoceros-horn-cup-and-was-auctioned-for-a75640-in-2013/articleshow/134656341.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-sydney-shopper-bought-a-carved-cup-for-a4-at-a-thrift-shop-experts-identified-it-as-a-centuries-old-chinese-rhinoceros-horn-cup-and-was-auctioned-for-a75640-in-2013/articleshow/134656341.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T10:55:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134656401,imgsize-239921.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US Marine arrested in Japan over murder, robbery of local woman]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134669676.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/us-marine-arrested-in-japan-over-murder-robbery-of-local-woman/articleshow/134669676.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/us-marine-arrested-in-japan-over-murder-robbery-of-local-woman/articleshow/134669676.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T10:15:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134669752,imgsize-62178.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trump leaks senator’s number after row over clock-change bill: What’s the dispute]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134669077.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Under the current system, Americans move their clocks one hour forward in March and one hour back in November. Moving the clock forward means sunrise and sunset appear one hour later on the clock. If the sun would normally rise at 7 am and set at 6 pm, the clock change would make them appear as 8 am and 7 pm. This gives people more daylight in the evening.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trump-leaks-senators-number-after-row-over-clock-change-bill-whats-the-dispute/articleshow/134669077.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trump-leaks-senators-number-after-row-over-clock-change-bill-whats-the-dispute/articleshow/134669077.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T08:52:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134669181,imgsize-70060.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Blatant lie’: China slams US panel’s ‘genocide’ claim after Starbucks opens first Xinjiang stores]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134669097.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[China's foreign ministry has condemned a US congressional committee's criticism of Starbucks for opening stores in Xinjiang. The US claims genocide against the Uyghur minority in the region, which China denies vehemently. Despite the accusations, Starbucks intends to continue its business operations in Xinjiang. The company recently expanded through a joint venture in China, increasing its nationwide presence.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/blatant-lie-china-slams-us-panels-genocide-claim-after-starbucks-opens-first-xinjiang-stores/articleshow/134669097.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/blatant-lie-china-slams-us-panels-genocide-claim-after-starbucks-opens-first-xinjiang-stores/articleshow/134669097.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T08:41:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134669142,imgsize-41282.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[ShinyHunters hacker in FBI data theft held in Jordan]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134668729.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/shinyhunters-hacker-in-fbi-data-theft-held-in-jordan/articleshow/134668729.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/shinyhunters-hacker-in-fbi-data-theft-held-in-jordan/articleshow/134668729.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T07:13:10+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134668764,imgsize-43460.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Tennessee prison chief Frank Strada resigns after Christa Pike's botched execution]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/pho